V5.0.1: [V50001] by Calamath
- The /cscript command now correctly outputs table-type elements via d() and df().
- Updated API version to 101047 (ESO 11.1.x : Feast of Shadows)

[Console version]
- the -v option is always enabled, displaying results in a dialog box instead of the chat window.
- The /cdiag command will show you the total amount of add-on memory used.


V5.0.0: [V50000] by Calamath
Overhaul to support console machines.
- Expanded support for the -v option.
- The scrolling operation of the output dialog is now compatible with the gamepad stick.
- The index number displayed in the add-on list was synchronized with the add-on index in the Add-on Manager.
- Removed the remaining advisory message services.
- Removed '/cdiag.reset' command.
- Discontinued the use of savedata.
- Updated API version to 101046 (ESO 11.0.x : Seasons of the Worm Cult Part 1)

V4.45.2: [V44502] by Calamath
- Fixed an issue where the /cscript command output dialog was broken after using the spinner control.

V4.45.1: [V44501] by Calamath
- Added /cscript command. This command is similar to /script, but displays the results of d() and df() in a dialog instead of the chat window.

V4.45.0: [V44500] by Calamath
- Added -v option to output result to the dialog box. Now you can copy the results to the clipboard.

